osm2pgsql
------------------------------------------
osm2pgsql is a tool for loading OpenStreetMap data into a PostgreSQL / PostGIS
database suitable for applications like rendering into a map, geocoding with
Nominatim, or general analysis.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libbz2_1-1.0.8-2
  libexpat1-2.10.0-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  liblua5.3-5.3.6-4
  libpq5-18.7-1
  libproj25-9.9.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  zlib0-1.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libboost-devel-1.66.0-1
  libbz2-devel-1.0.8-2
  libexpat-devel-2.10.0-1
  liblua-devel-5.3.6-4
  libpq-devel-18.7-1
  libpq5-18.7-1
  libproj-devel-9.9.0-1
  lua-5.3.6-4
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  nlohmann_json-3.12.0-1bl3
  proj-9.9.0-1
  zlib-devel-1.4-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/osm2pgsql-dev/osm2pgsql

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/osm2pgsql-dev/osm2pgsql/archive/refs/tags/2.3.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack osm2pgsql-2.3.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./osm2pgsql-2.3.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/osm2pgsql-2.3.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/osm2pgsql-2.3.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

